# Native fragments and accumulate-once for the 16-row tile on gfx1100. Where the form/NT/chain record
# qualifies (kNative) the token rows load as their 16 K bytes in natural order (the same address in lane
# and lane + 16), the weight rows read back from the wave's LDS tile in the same order, and the int32
# sum of a 128-K scale group stays in the gfx11 layout until the float fold: no operand exchange at all.
# The other specialisations keep the compatibility form (eight bytes a step, as before).
@@ find 1
